A bubbletea + lipgloss TUI generated from `~/scripts/tui-cli-template/go/`. It
ships a working **item manager** demo so you have real patterns to adapt rather
than empty stubs.

## Build & run

```bash
make build              # → bin/{{PROJECT_NAME}}  (injects version via ldflags)
./bin/{{PROJECT_NAME}}
# or, during development:
make run
make test
```

## What it does (the demo)

- **Home** — add items, **live search/filter**, a scrolling list, and a Config entry.
  - Tab / Shift+Tab cycle focus: Add field → Filter field → list.
  - In the list: ↑/↓ (or j/k) select · Enter/c copy to clipboard · x delete · o Config · q quit.
  - **Ctrl+C quits from anywhere** (q only quits while the list is focused — it
    types into the Add/Filter fields otherwise).
- **Config** — an Options screen editing `~/.config/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.conf`:
  inline text edit, a **radio overlay** (Theme), a **bool toggle** (Confirm delete),
  "Edit config in $EDITOR", and "Reload from disk". The file is comment-preserving
  and round-trip safe, so hand-edits survive.

## Structure

```
cmd/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/main.go   — entry point; sets app name/description, calls tui.Run
internal/tui/app.go            — model, screen dispatch, async load, Run()
internal/tui/home.go           — home dashboard (add / search / list / delete)
internal/tui/options.go        — settings screen (edit / radio / toggle / $EDITOR)
internal/tui/config.go         — Config struct, Fields table, load/save
internal/tui/parse.go          — round-trip KEY="value" config parser
internal/tui/store.go          — JSON item store (~/.local/share/{{PROJECT_NAME}}/)
internal/tui/style.go          — palette + named lipgloss styles
internal/tui/banner.go         — banner: name · description · version · byline
internal/tui/util.go           — clipboard, atomic write, list-scroll window
internal/tui/app_test.go       — table of model/render/round-trip tests
```

## Make it yours

1. Edit the four demo settings in `config.go` (`Fields` + `Config` + `fromMap`/`toMap`/`applyEdit`).
2. Replace the `[]string` items in `store.go` and `home.go` with your domain type.
3. Add screens by extending the `screen` enum in `app.go` and adding `update*`/`view*` methods.

Tests call `Update`/`View` directly (no `tea.NewProgram`) — the Elm architecture
makes the whole app testable without a terminal. Follow that pattern.
